<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-soc> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation> "EU DPP Textile Ontology - Textile Substances of Concern Module. Version 1.1.2."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-soc> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-07-09"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-soc> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Elio Hbeich"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-soc> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Textile-sector specialisation of the EU DPP Substances of Concern ontology. It specialises substance presence, product location, concentration reporting, product-group qualification, thresholds and lifecycle handling for textile products."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-soc> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026-07-09"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-soc> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-soc> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-07-16"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-soc> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1781/oj> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-soc> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-soc> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-soc> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "EU DPP Textile Ontology - Textile Substances of Concern Module"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-soc> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix> "txtsoc" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-soc> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespaceUri> "https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-soc#" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-soc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This module does not classify every textile chemical as a substance of concern. It specialises the generic SoC presence-context model for textile products and attaches textile-specific information to the occurrence, not globally to the chemical identity."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-soc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Textile substances of concern ontology"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-soc> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "Version 1.1.2" .
